// Construction materials, imported from the OSRS cache by tools/models/importosrs.py.
// Every model re-encoded by osrs2ob2.py and round-trip verified; all five rendered and looked at
// before shipping - four planks that read as planks in four different woods, and a saw.
//
// None of these is equipment with combat bonuses, so the importer's usual by-hand block is answered
// rather than left: no category, no params, no equip requirement. The saw's wear slot came out of
// the cache.
//
// Plank cost is 100 because OSRS obj 960 carries no cost at all - the other three do (250 / 500 /
// 1500), and those are exactly what the sawmill charges to cut one.
//
// Imported from a modern OSRS cache by tools/models/importosrs.py.
// Models are RE-ENCODED from OSRS model format into the 317-family format
// (tools/models/osrs2ob2.py); every one is round-trip verified before writing.
// wearpos/wearpos2/wearpos3 come from the cache - do not hand-edit them.

// NOT IN USE, and must not be brought back into use. 377 already has a plank - obj 960,
// `woodplank`, name "Plank", desc "A plank of wood!" - and this import added a second obj with the
// same name and the same description. The two are indistinguishable in the inventory and in the
// bank, and nothing reconciles them.
//
// That duplication silently broke three quests. The sawmill operator is the only repeatable,
// advertised plank source in the game, and it handed out THIS obj, while Observatory Quest
// (observatory_professor.rs2), Horror from the Deep's bridge (quest_horror.rs2) and Dragon Slayer's
// hull patch (lady_lumbridge.rs2) all check `woodplank`. A player could buy planks, carry them to
// the Professor, and be told "Sorry, not yet. Three planks was it?" with three planks in hand.
//
// Three more had it the other way round: In Search of the Myreque's ladder rungs, In Aid of the
// Myreque's Burgh de Rott repairs and Swan Song's palisade checked for THIS obj, which after the
// sawmill fix nothing hands out, so no plank at all got a player through them. The two Myreque
// quests take `woodplank` now; Swan Song's wall takes iron sheets off Franklin's press, as in 2006.
//
// The sawmill, every poh_furn_mat row and both Myreque quests now use `woodplank`. The definition is
// kept only because
// pack/obj.pack allocates the id and a name in the pack with no definition is a build error.
[plank]
name=Plank
desc=A plank of wood!
model=obj_plank
2dxan=356
2dyan=148
2dyof=18
weight=800g
cost=100

[oak_plank]
name=Oak plank
desc=A plank of sturdy oak.
model=obj_oak_plank
2dxan=356
2dyan=148
2dyof=18
recol1s=19910
recol1d=21036
recol2s=7329
recol2d=14662
weight=800g
cost=250
members=yes

[teak_plank]
name=Teak plank
desc=A plank of fine teak.
model=obj_teak_plank
2dxan=356
2dyan=148
2dyof=18
recol1s=19910
recol1d=14695
recol2s=7329
recol2d=10467
